implementationPlan.description:
TESTS FIRST (red). Load test-driven-development.

The producer is CQ-I03a (task-c0b0775f, a dependency): scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs. It is landed by WORKING time; adapt to its landed field names and codes, which planningNotes lists as assumed.

Create moe-jetbrains/src/test/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/ManagedVmPresentationTest.kt (JUnit 4, headless), in the style of AccountPresentationTest.kt and DeliveryPresentationTest.kt. Keep it to about 130 lines, with parameterized tables and helpers. Assert exact keys, args, rows and action booleans; never truthiness.

Cases:
- P1, readiness separation (DoD 1):
  - a status report with provider.ready true and executionReady/verified false gives three distinct lines: PROVIDER_READY, EXECUTION_NOT_READY and NOT_VERIFIED;
  - provider ready with executionReady or verified absent, null, "true" (a string) or 1 still gives EXECUTION_NOT_READY and NOT_VERIFIED. Only a literal JSON true counts, and provider readiness never implies either;
  - provider not ready gives PROVIDER_NOT_READY with its code.
- P2, owned only (DoD 2):
  - rows equal the report's instances, in order, and nothing else;
  - an instance name failing R06's owned-name shape (lifecycle.mjs OWNED_NAME_PREFIX plus its random suffix), or a duplicated name, makes the WHOLE report Unreadable, failing closed;
  - ManagedVmCommand.args(command) is exactly [script, 'status'|'reconcile'|'cleanup', '--project', basePath]. The API has no instance parameter at all.
- P3, actions:
  - refresh is enabled whenever nothing runs;
  - reconcile and cleanup only when the last status was readable with provider ready, and cleanup only with at least 1 instance;
  - every action is disabled while a run is in flight (single flight);
  - an Unreadable state allows only refresh.
- P4, strong profile (DoD 3): for EVERY report, including one claiming executionReady:true and verified:true, strongProfile is Blocked(STRONG_PROFILE_BLOCKED). ManagedVmActions holds exactly refresh, reconcile and cleanup: no activation entry.
- P5, report and refusal mapping:
  - a cleanup report renders deleted, preserved (each with its reason) and errors (each with its fixed code);
  - each known code maps to its key, with the code as an arg;
  - an unknown code maps to UNKNOWN_CODE plus the code;
  - non-JSON, more than one line, more than 64 KiB, an unknown schema, a nonzero exit or a timeout give Unreadable(key), never the raw text or stderr.

Run `cd moe-jetbrains && ./gradlew test --tests com.moe.toolwindow.ManagedVmPresentationTest`. It fails before step 2 exists (use the Windows equivalent of step 4 if WSL has no JDK).

Create moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/ManagedVmPresentation.kt. It is pure, with no Swing and no IO, about 110 lines, and mirrors AccountPresentation.kt's shape.

- `data class ManagedVmText(val key: String, val args: List<Any> = emptyList())`.
- `data class ManagedVmRow(instance, phase, state, launchTries, taskId)`.
- `data class ManagedVmActions(val refresh: Boolean, val reconcile: Boolean, val cleanup: Boolean)`.
- `object ManagedVmKeys`, with every bundle key:
  - TAB 'moe.tab.managedVms';
  - PROVIDER_READY, PROVIDER_NOT_READY, EXECUTION_NOT_READY, EXECUTION_READY, NOT_VERIFIED, VERIFIED;
  - STRONG_PROFILE_BLOCKED, UNREADABLE, UNKNOWN_CODE;
  - one key per I03a code;
  - the column and button keys.
- `enum class ManagedVmCommand { STATUS, RECONCILE, CLEANUP }`, with `fun args(script: String, basePath: String): List<String>`. There is no instance parameter.
- `sealed interface ManagedVmReport`: Status, Reconcile, Cleanup and Unreadable(key).
- `object ManagedVmPresentation`:
  - decode(stdout, exitCode, timedOut): Gson over a JsonReader with lenient parsing OFF;
  - readiness(report): the three lines;
  - strongProfile(report): always Blocked(STRONG_PROFILE_BLOCKED);
  - rows(report);
  - actions(lastStatus, running).

Error handling: decode never throws. Every malformed, foreign-named, duplicated, oversized, multi-line, unknown-schema, nonzero-exit or timed-out output is Unreadable with a fixed key. Raw stdout or stderr never reaches a ManagedVmText.

The KDoc states:
- provider readiness is not execution readiness or verification;
- the IDE never offers strong-profile activation, because the daemon refuses verified-local with EXECUTION_PROFILE_NOT_READY;
- ownership is the producer's ledger, and the IDE never names an instance.

Make P1-P5 pass.

The Swing tab and its wiring. Report every file in modifiedFiles.

1. Create moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/ManagedVmPanel.kt (about 90 lines, Disposable):
   - three readiness labels and the strong-profile line;
   - a JBTable of rows;
   - Refresh, Reconcile and Clean up owned buttons, each enabled from ManagedVmPresentation.actions;
   - a note area for the last report's preserved and errors entries.
   Each button runs ManagedVmCommand through a Task.Backgroundable using the platform's CapturingProcessHandler(GeneralCommandLine(node + args).withCharset(UTF_8)).runProcessWithProgressIndicator(indicator, timeoutMs):
   - timeoutMs is 120s for status and reconcile and 20 min for cleanup;
   - cancellation kills the process;
   - only stdout and the exit code reach decode; stderr is ignored;
   - render on the EDT;
   - single flight.
   Clean up owned first shows a confirmation naming the producer's rule: only Moe-owned VMs whose attempt is closed and whose lease is free. Refresh runs once when the tab is shown.
2. moe-jetbrains/src/main/kotlin/com/moe/toolwindow/MoeToolWindowPanel.kt: addTab(MoeBundle.message(ManagedVmKeys.TAB), managedVmPanel) after the Accounts tab, plus Disposer.register(this, managedVmPanel).
3. moe-jetbrains/src/main/resources/messages/MoeBundle.properties: every ManagedVmKeys key, as plain text with no HTML, giving actionable wording. Example: 'Strong profile (verified-local) is unavailable: protected isolation, trusted runner evidence and revision-bound delivery are not certified.'
4. The script path: make TerminalAgentLauncher.resolveBundledPath internal and call it with 'scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs', which build.gradle.kts already bundles under local-runner/**. A missing script shows UNREADABLE with SCRIPT_MISSING, and no process starts.
5. node: resolve it exactly as MoeDaemonSupervisor does for the project's RuntimeSelectionPolicy profile, at about line 235. Reach the existing resolver through the project's supervisor instance if one is reachable; otherwise hoist resolveNodeExecutable into the companion without behavior change (MoeDaemonSupervisorTest stays green). If node is unresolved, show NODE_MISSING and start no process.

Error handling: every process failure renders a fixed key; nothing blocks the EDT; dispose cancels a running task.

VERIFY ONCE. Edit only what this step's findings need, and report it in modifiedFiles.

1. Mutants. Apply each to a scratch copy, restore it, then cmp. Each must fail the named case:
   - derive execution readiness from provider readiness: P1;
   - accept a string "true": P1;
   - add an instance argument to a command, or accept a foreign name: P2;
   - enable cleanup while running: P3;
   - let strongProfile follow report.verified: P4;
   - put stderr or raw stdout into a message: P5.
2. The GATE: `cd moe-jetbrains && ./gradlew test` must exit 0.
   - WSL has no JDK. As CQ-I02's QA did, hold the 'jetbrains-gradle' lease (moe.acquire_resource, then release_resource) and run the Windows equivalent: `cmd.exe /d /c "set GRADLE_OPTS=-Xmx512m&& cd /d D:\projexts\moes\moe-jetbrains && .\gradlew.bat test --rerun"`.
   - Supply both the pinned command and the one actually run.
   - Read the result XMLs to confirm that ManagedVmPresentationTest ran, with its counts, and that no suite failed.
3. Size: `git diff --numstat` over moe-jetbrains must be at most 400 net (QA cap; tests count).
4. A red suite outside this task is compared against the same run on a tree WITHOUT this task's files. Never edit peer files.
5. Supply the command, its exit code and the output tail to complete_task.

ADVERSARIAL SELF-REVIEW, once, as the last step. Load adversarial-self-review. Read the diff as a user, or a buggy producer, trying to get the IDE to act on a VM Moe does not own or to suggest a strong profile it cannot run:
- a foreign or duplicated name in the report;
- a report that claims readiness or verification;
- a double click, or a dispose mid-run;
- a huge, hanging or stderr-flooding producer;
- a missing script or node;
- paths with spaces and Windows drive letters in GeneralCommandLine. Arguments are passed as a list, never through a shell;
- whether the panel writes .moe or sends UPDATE_SETTINGS. It must do neither: I02's PlanApprovalContractTest pins UPDATE_SETTINGS to four keys.
Also check JetBrains threading (no EDT IO) and that every string comes from MoeBundle.

Then write the Serena memory 'task-task-63930ba4a46344f9af3c41cfef60ae0d-handoff' for CQ-I05 (VS Code parity) and CQ-I06. Cover:
- the presentation contract: keys, actions, the owned-name rule and Unreadable cases;
- the process seam: CapturingProcessHandler, timeouts and single flight;
- that I05 must mirror the same three readiness lines and the no-activation rule.

planningNotes.codebaseInsights:
Assumed I03a contract, from its task description:
- `node scripts/local-runner/vm-control.mjs <status|reconcile|cleanup> --project <abs>` prints ONE JSON line (at most 64 KiB) and exits 0 for every report; usage errors print VM_CONTROL_INPUT_INVALID and exit 2;
- status: {schema:'moe-vm-status-v1', provider:{ready, code?, platform?}, executionReady:false, verified:false, instances:[{instance, phase, state, launchTries, taskId}], invalid};
- reconcile: schema 'moe-vm-reconcile-v1', the reconcileOwned report;
- cleanup: schema 'moe-vm-cleanup-v1', the cleanupOwned report {deleted, preserved:[{instance, reason}], errors:[{instance, code}], invalid};
- owned names follow lifecycle.mjs OWNED_NAME_PREFIX 'moe-vm-' plus a random suffix (isOwnedInstanceName).

Verified JetBrains facts:
- the AccountsPanel/AccountPresentation pattern (Text/Row/Actions/Keys/Presentation objects, tested headless);
- MoeToolWindowPanel addTab at about line 306;
- MoeBundle.properties;
- TerminalAgentLauncher.resolveBundledPath is private, at about line 789;
- build.gradle.kts bundles scripts/local-runner/**, excluding tests;
- MoeDaemonSupervisor.resolveNodeExecutable is a class member (about line 429), used with a protected-PATH variant at about line 235;
- WSL has no JDK. CQ-I02's QA ran the Windows gradlew under the 'jetbrains-gradle' lease.
